    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) and **Andy Pages** (74.42), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Sugano. **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier start, boasting a +19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s xERA and a generous +14% park factor, positioning him as an elite threat to clear fences. **Drake Baldwin** (71.20) also surges into the lineup; hitting leadoff against Ober provides a massive volume cushion, and his strong xwOBA profile suggests he is primed to exploit the 4.81 xERA matchup. While **Gunnar Henderson** (50.62) and **Coby Mayo** (52.72) face a tougher road against a high-caliber arm in McClanahan, their high floors and favorable lineup positioning keep them as staples in the core rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the marginal group, specifically **Liam Hicks** (51.97) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.60). While **Luis Robert Jr.** brings the elite sprint speed we covet for our 5x5 scarcity strategy, his dynamic platoon penalty against Buehler tempered his ceiling, resulting in a narrow margin over other options. We are effectively playing the \"BvP/Park\" lottery today, as the 4.50+ xERA for opponents facing **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Drake Baldwin** represents our best path to meaningful R and RBI accumulation. We remain vigilant regarding the health of our depth, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. Monitor weather reports for the McClanahan start, as any wind shifts could further depress the already marginal output expected from **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**.",
